  "summary": "Malicious code in npm-wold (npm)",
  "details": "The package npm-wold@1.1.1 is a trojanized object-utility library. Its postinstall hook (dist/config.js) fetches a payload from my-api[.]trade-api[.]workers[.]dev?id=4 and dynamically executes the response using globalThis[data.success](data.id), enabling arbitrary remote code execution on the installer's machine at install time. The bundled flatten/path utility code is a decoy.",
